Z||000011||LT1 Chop Top||08-16-2001||04:51 PM||||Falcon,<P>Trust me....a chop top IS fun!||||reg||12
Z||000012||Archie||08-16-2001||07:42 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>Falcon,<P>Trust me....a chop top IS fun!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Like he said the Chop Top is fun!<P>Before I say anything else, let it be clear that I am not the one selling this car and I have nothing to gain or lose if it sells or not. Mrs. Warber is the owner and it is being sold on her behalf by a family friend.<P>Now that that's been said. <P>This car is a Shoe-in throphy winner. You should be able to show it anywhere at any type of show and take home more hardware than you can carry, I recommend you leave your passenger at home.<P>Mrs. Warber has had this car stored in her garage every since Rich died. It's been taken out for a bit of exercize but I'm sure it hasn't had 100 miles in the last 2 years.<P>When Rich died, I was sure (and still am sure) that if properly marketed that car should be worth &gt;$20K. You know that $20K won't buy you much in either the show car world or at any car dealer. Hower to properly market it you need to take it out of the garage and let it be seen.<P>There is no way in heck that anyone could build that car for the $16K they are asking for it. Hell, if I did a V-8 swap to a STOCK 86 GT using that engine and all the chrome etc. it would run you close to $16K. <P>I think that the Blue Chop Top looks better, but if the price on this car gets much lower, I'm gonna be buying it.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroKyle||08-16-2001||09:39 PM||||I'll donate 1000 bucks if you let me have it for 6 weekends of a year and paint it black.||||reg||1
Z||000014||NIFE [PaulV]||08-16-2001||10:14 PM||||I can tell you that I have driven this car. Not a long way, but far enough to feel the power of Rich's handbuilt V8!! At the price Rich's wife would now take, its a bargain. Rich Warber was a real craftsman and mechanic. He did all the work himself including the fiberglass work to give the 86GT a different "look". Now is a great time for someone to take home this prize. Its a show winner right out of the box.||||reg||1
Z||000015||artherd||08-17-2001||04:21 AM||||$20k a lot ?!?!  Pardon my french, but that's just wrong.<P>This car for $40k is a steal.  Think about it, it's a BETTER car in every way than anything you can buy under $50,000.<P>Somebody fricking buy it already (one of you guys that could afford a new Porsche or so, you know, the ones the liberals or conservatives or whoever cares about, we now know you're out there, and you're loaded :)<P>The PPE is indeed awesome awesome awesome.  I'd buy it myself if it were 88 based and I didn't want to make my 'own' vision.<P>Archie, picking up this car wouldn't be too bad a move, talk about a rooling demo for us all to slobber over!<P>(LT1 Chop Top, you can't have it, you already have one, be nice and share, grin!)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NIFE [PaulV]:<BR><B>I can tell you that I have driven this car. Not a long way, but far enough to feel the power of Rich's handbuilt V8!! At the price Rich's wife would now take, its a bargain. Rich Warber was a real craftsman and mechanic. He did all the work himself including the fiberglass work to give the 86GT a different "look". Now is a great time for someone to take home this prize. Its a show winner right out of the box.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
